      "body": "### Problem\n\nNeovim crashes with\r\n```c++\r\n#0  __pthread_kill_implementation (threadid=<optimized out>, signo=signo@entry=6, no_tid=no_tid@entry=0) at ./nptl/pthread_kill.c:44\r\n#1  0x00007fd98d32dd2f in __pthread_kill_internal (signo=6, threadid=<optimized out>) at ./nptl/pthread_kill.c:78\r\n#2  0x00007fd98d2deef2 in __GI_raise (sig=sig@entry=6) at ../sysdeps/posix/raise.c:26\r\n#3  0x00007fd98d2c9472 in __GI_abort () at ./stdlib/abort.c:79\r\n#4  0x00007fd98d3222d0 in __libc_message (action=action@entry=do_abort, fmt=fmt@entry=0x7fd98d43c459 \"%s\\n\") at ../sysdeps/posix/libc_fatal.c:155\r\n#5  0x00007fd98d33764a in malloc_printerr (str=str@entry=0x7fd98d43f0a8 \"free(): invalid next size (fast)\") at ./malloc/malloc.c:5660\r\n#6  0x00007fd98d3394ba in _int_free (av=0x7fd98d475c60 <main_arena>, p=0x55c12ce52200, have_lock=have_lock@entry=0) at ./malloc/malloc.c:4518\r\n#7  0x00007fd98d33bd2f in __GI___libc_free (mem=<optimized out>) at ./malloc/malloc.c:3385\r\n#8  0x000055c12b556d45 in xfree (ptr=0x55c12ce52210) at .../src/nvim/memory.c:134\r\n#9  0x000055c12b654509 in stl_alloc_click_defs (cdp=0x55c12ce52210, width=7, size=0x55c12ce71270) at .../src/nvim/statusline.c:243\r\n#10 0x000055c12b6568fc in build_statuscol_str (wp=0x55c12ce6e8b0, lnum=156, relnum=0, stcp=0x7ffe2b62c5d0) at .../src/nvim/statusline.c:908\r\n#11 0x000055c12b42012e in get_statuscol_str (wp=0x55c12ce6e8b0, lnum=156, virtnum=0, stcp=0x7ffe2b62c5d0) at .../src/nvim/drawline.c:697\r\n#12 0x000055c12b42317b in win_line (wp=0x55c12ce6e8b0, lnum=156, startrow=0, endrow=14, number_only=false, spv=0x7ffe2b62d930, foldinfo=..., providers=0x7ffe2b62d970, provider_err=0x55c12b922df0 <provider_err>)\r\nat .../src/nvim/drawline.c:1727\r\n#13 0x000055c12b42d36f in win_update (wp=0x55c12ce6e8b0, providers=0x7ffe2b62da30) at .../src/nvim/drawscreen.c:2238\r\n#14 0x000055c12b428b6f in update_screen () at .../src/nvim/drawscreen.c:632\r\n#15 0x000055c12b57a3bc in normal_redraw (s=0x7ffe2b62db50) at .../src/nvim/normal.c:1321\r\n#16 0x000055c12b57a60e in normal_check (state=0x7ffe2b62db50) at .../src/nvim/normal.c:1414\r\n#17 0x000055c12b6533f9 in state_enter (s=0x7ffe2b62db50) at .../src/nvim/state.c:40\r\n#18 0x000055c12b57822b in normal_enter (cmdwin=false, noexmode=false) at .../src/nvim/normal.c:501\r\n#19 0x000055c12b3739cc in main (argc=4, argv=0x7ffe2b62df78) at .../src/nvim/main.c:641\r\n```\r\n\r\n@luukvbaal \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAt the moment it occurs for me with statusline.nvim plugin and lua-language-server. I suspect this happens while adding diagnostics but currently I cannot find any simply way to reproduce it.  Maybe I'm wrong in assuming that the backtrace alone can be useful. Please close this issue if you consider it useless. I'll add steps if I find the reproducible way in the future. \n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo crash\n\n### Neovim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-584+g0ca2d11c1\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nDebian Sid\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.26.5-5, tmux 3.3a-4\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ntmux-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
